cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BIG — Bitcoin Incentivized Grading"
message: "If you use BIG or build on its design, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Maali
    given-names: Marvin Kenneth
    affiliation: "GradeScript UG"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MarvinMK-bit/BIG"
abstract: >-
  An automated grading system for handwritten student scripts, designed
  to require progressively less large language model inference over time.
  Grading runs down two comparable paths — an LLM grader and a
  deterministic, versioned mark scheme — writing results into a shared
  per-question schema so the two can be measured against each other.
  Contributors are rewarded in bitcoin over the Lightning Network for
  feedback and for authoring mark schemes.
keywords:
  - automated grading
  - assessment
  - bitcoin
  - lightning network
  - deterministic grading
  - education technology
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: "2026-09-13"
version: "0.1.0"
